    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for dpdk",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for dpdk fixes the following issues:\n\nUpdate to version 24.11.4.\n\nSecurity issues fixed:\n\n- CVE-2025-23259: issue in the Poll Mode Driver (PMD) allows an attacker on a VM in the system to leak information and\n  cause a denial of service on the network interface (bsc#1254161).\n\nOther issues fixed:\n\n- Remove obsolete build option -Denable_kmods.\n- Add \"which\" as a build requirement.\n- Drop pesign and needssslcertforbuild because we don't build a kmp anymore (bsc#1247389).\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "details",
        "text": "openSUSE-Leap-16.0-233",
        "title": "Patchnames"
      },
